# WARNO Unraid repository

This repo is an Unraid template plus a settings wrapper around `eugensystems/warno`. Leave server settings, launch arguments, and published defaults unchanged unless the task asks for that change.

## Template

- Edit `templates/warno-dedicated-server.xml` for the container and `ca_profile.xml` for the Community Apps profile.
- Use `<Container version="2">`. Express paths and variables as one-line `<Config>` entries. Leave out legacy `<Networking>`, `<Data>`, and `<Environment>` blocks.
- `Type="Path"` maps a host folder. `Type="Variable"` sets an environment variable. Set `Mask="true"` on secrets.
- This server uses `<Network>host</Network>`. The game port is `EXPOSEDPORT`, forwarded as TCP and UDP. There is no Docker port mapping.
- Keep Overview, Description, and `README.md` in agreement.

## Evidence

- Cite a source URL for Eugen or Docker Hub claims. Label anything not checked in this session as unverified.
- `10400` is this repo's default game port. Eugen's docs show a placeholder port.
- A parsed XML file is only well-formed. Unraid behavior still needs a server test.
- `entrypoint-unraid.sh` writes settings, then runs `/server/entrypoint2.sh`. Leave Eugen's server arguments in their image.

## Secrets

- Keep Eugen logins, dedicated keys, `login.ini`, and real `settings/` directories out of git, examples, issues, and chat.
- Samples may use `YOUR_EUGEN_LOGIN_HERE` and `YOUR_EUGEN_DEDICATED_KEY_HERE` only.
- A key that reaches git history stays compromised after a later delete.

## Validation and git

- After template, entrypoint, or check changes, run `sh scripts/check_repo.sh`.
- Tests must not start the real WARNO server.
- Commit only when asked. Do not push to `main`, force-push, deploy, publish the image, or merge a pull request unless explicitly asked.
